\title{Free Time Slots}
\maketitle

\section{Overview}

The program reads booked time slots from standard input, one per line in the
form [[09:00-10:30]], and prints the free slots of the working day
08:00--17:00 in the same format.  Bookings may overlap, touch, arrive in any
order, and may extend outside the working day.

The approach: convert times to minutes, sort the bookings by start, sweep
through the day keeping a cursor at the end of the last covered minute, and
emit a gap whenever the next booking starts after the cursor.

