\section{Parsing and formatting}

Times are represented as minutes since midnight.  Blank lines are ignored.
Malformed lines raise [[ValueError]].

<<constants>>=
DAY_START = 8 * 60
DAY_END = 17 * 60
@

<<parsing>>=
def parse_time(text):
    """Convert 'HH:MM' to minutes since midnight."""
    hours, minutes = text.strip().split(":")
    h, m = int(hours), int(minutes)
    if not (0 <= h <= 24 and 0 <= m < 60) or (h == 24 and m != 0):
        raise ValueError(f"invalid time: {text!r}")
    return h * 60 + m


def parse_slot(line):
    """Convert 'HH:MM-HH:MM' to a (start, end) pair of minutes."""
    start, end = line.strip().split("-")
    s, e = parse_time(start), parse_time(end)
    if e < s:
        raise ValueError(f"slot ends before it starts: {line!r}")
    return s, e
@

<<formatting>>=
def format_time(minutes):
    return f"{minutes // 60:02d}:{minutes % 60:02d}"


def format_slot(slot):
    return f"{format_time(slot[0])}-{format_time(slot[1])}"
@

\section{Computing the free slots}

Sorting by start time lets one pass find the gaps.  [[cursor]] is the first
minute not yet known to be booked; a booking starting after it exposes a free
gap.  Using [[max]] for the cursor handles overlapping and nested bookings,
and a booking starting exactly at the cursor (touching) leaves no gap.

<<computing free slots>>=
def free_slots(bookings, day_start=DAY_START, day_end=DAY_END):
    """Return the list of free (start, end) gaps within the working day."""
    free = []
    cursor = day_start
    for start, end in sorted(bookings):
        if start > cursor:
            free.append((cursor, min(start, day_end)))
        cursor = max(cursor, end)
        if cursor >= day_end:
            break
    if cursor < day_end:
        free.append((cursor, day_end))
    return free
@

A booking that starts after the day ends would give a gap beyond the end, but
the [[min]] and the early [[break]] prevent that: once the cursor reaches
[[day_end]] we stop, and a gap is clipped to [[day_end]].  Bookings entirely
before the day start only move the cursor forward from [[day_start]] via
[[max]], so they have no effect.

\section{Main program}

<<main>>=
def main():
    bookings = [parse_slot(line) for line in sys.stdin if line.strip()]
    for slot in free_slots(bookings):
        print(format_slot(slot))
@

\section{Tests}

<<test_freeslots.py>>=
import io
import pytest
import freeslots
from freeslots import free_slots, parse_slot, format_slot


def run(*lines):
    return [format_slot(s) for s in free_slots([parse_slot(l) for l in lines])]


<<tests>>
@

<<tests>>=
def test_no_bookings():
    assert run() == ["08:00-17:00"]

def test_single_booking_middle():
    assert run("09:00-10:30") == ["08:00-09:00", "10:30-17:00"]

def test_touching():
    assert run("08:00-09:00", "09:00-10:00") == ["10:00-17:00"]

def test_overlapping_unordered():
    assert run("11:00-12:00", "09:00-11:30", "10:00-10:30") == [
        "08:00-09:00", "12:00-17:00"]

def test_nested():
    assert run("09:00-15:00", "10:00-11:00") == ["08:00-09:00", "15:00-17:00"]

def test_fully_booked():
    assert run("07:00-18:00") == []

def test_outside_day_ignored():
    assert run("06:00-07:00", "18:00-19:00") == ["08:00-17:00"]

def test_partially_outside():
    assert run("07:00-09:00", "16:00-18:00") == ["09:00-16:00"]

def test_gap_between_bookings():
    assert run("08:00-09:00", "10:00-17:00") == ["09:00-10:00"]

def test_bad_input():
    with pytest.raises(ValueError):
        parse_slot("25:00-26:00")
    with pytest.raises(ValueError):
        parse_slot("10:00-09:00")

def test_main(monkeypatch, capsys):
    monkeypatch.setattr("sys.stdin", io.StringIO("09:00-10:00\n\n13:00-14:00\n"))
    freeslots.main()
    assert capsys.readouterr().out.splitlines() == [
        "08:00-09:00", "10:00-13:00", "14:00-17:00"]
